+/*
+ * laurel 2101: surface memory without a contiguous run. On the 4 KiB-page kernel a surface buffer is 16 KiB
+ * aligned (SWEET_UPAGE: user tasks have 16 KiB pages), and an IOBufferMemoryDescriptor alignment above
+ * page_size makes it physically contiguous (IOBufferMemoryDescriptor.cpp: "alignment > page_size" adds
+ * kIOMemoryPhysicallyContiguous). Every surface the GPU does not touch then needed one contiguous run:
+ * with fragmented RAM even a 4.8 MB one failed. A pageable buffer is its own VM object (offset 0, so a 16 KiB
+ * user page never shows a neighbour), its pages are wired by prepare() for the surface's life (the
